│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Main ideas:                                                                               │
│                          │ - Replace several absolute/long-horizon features with shorter-window versions (5–20       │
│                          │ bars).                                                                                    │
│                          │ - Add rolling z-score normalization for returns, volume, volatility, and range so the     │
│                          │ model learns relative state rather than raw magnitude.                                    │
│                          │ - Add trend-of-regime features such as volatility change and autocorrelation change,      │
│                          │ which capture whether market character is shifting.                                       │
│                          │ - Add a momentum × volatility-regime interaction using a shorter momentum window.         │
│                          │ - Strengthen XGBoost regularization slightly and reduce tree count so it favors robust    │
│                          │ patterns over train-only idiosyncrasies.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should help reduce slope collapse on validation while also improving prediction      │
│                          │ dispersion, which is currently too low.                                                   │
