│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_regime_ensemble                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ This approach fundamentally reimagines the problem as a regime-detection + ensemble       │
│                          │ strategy rather than a single global model. The key insights:                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Regime Clustering**: Instead of trying to learn one model across all market          │
│                          │ conditions, we first cluster the training data into distinct market regimes using         │
│                          │ unsupervised learning (K-means on volatility/trend/volume features).                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Regime-Specific Models**: Train separate lightweight XGBoost models for each regime. │
│                          │ Each specialist model learns patterns specific to its regime, avoiding the generalization │
│                          │ collapse.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Adaptive Feature Sets**: Each regime gets a custom feature set optimized for that    │
│                          │ market condition:                                                                         │
│                          │    - High-vol regimes: short-term momentum, volatility ratios                             │
│                          │    - Low-vol regimes: mean reversion, microstructure                                      │
│                          │    - Trending regimes: trend-following indicators                                         │
│                          │    - Ranging regimes: support/resistance features                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Rolling Normalization**: All features are z-scored within short rolling windows      │
│                          │ (20-bar) to make them regime-invariant at the raw level, then regime-specific patterns    │
│                          │ are learned.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 5. **Ensemble Weighting**: At prediction time, compute regime probabilities using a       │
│                          │ softmax over distances to regime centroids, then blend predictions from all regime models │
│                          │ weighted by these probabilities.                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 6. **Shorter Lookbacks**: Features use max 20-bar lookbacks (5 hours) instead of 60+      │
│                          │ bars, making them more robust to regime shifts.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This solves the core problem: the model no longer tries to learn a single set of patterns │
│                          │ that work everywhere (which collapses on val). Instead, it learns multiple specialized    │
│                          │ patterns and adaptively selects which to use based on current market conditions.          │
