│ patch_description        │ This version is inspired by the prior program’s broad technical-indicator style, but it   │
│                          │ takes a different route: instead of stacking many long-horizon absolute indicators, it    │
│                          │ builds a compact set of short-lookback, regime-normalized, and trend-of-regime features   │
│                          │ designed to survive market shifts.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key novelty is a two-layer feature design:                                            │
│                          │ 1. Local normalization: returns, momentum, range, and volume are converted into rolling   │
│                          │ z-scores or percentile-like ranks using only past data, making features more              │
│                          │ regime-invariant across volatility changes.                                               │
│                          │ 2. Regime dynamics: rather than relying on static level features, it emphasizes the rate  │
│                          │ of change of volatility, efficiency, autocorrelation, and trend persistence. This targets │
│                          │ the failure mode where the model learned train-specific regime patterns that collapsed in │
│                          │ validation.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It also adds a small number of multiplicative interactions such as momentum × volatility  │
│                          │ regime and trend × efficiency, which often generalize better than raw levels alone. On    │
│                          │ the model side, the XGBoost configuration is made more conservative and robust: shallower │
│                          │ trees, stronger regularization, and higher min_child_weight to reduce reliance on brittle │
│                          │ training-only structure while preserving useful signal. The overall feature count stays   │
│                          │ well below the limit and all transformations use only past information.                   │
