│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the exact failure mode: the model’s slope collapses out-of-sample       │
│                          │ because it leans too much on absolute levels that shift across regimes. I’m making the    │
│                          │ feature set more regime-invariant by:                                                     │
│                          │ - replacing some long-horizon absolute features with shorter lookbacks,                   │
│                          │ - adding rolling z-score versions of key signals,                                         │
│                          │ - adding rate-of-change features for volatility, efficiency, and autocorrelation,         │
│                          │ - adding a momentum × volatility interaction on a short horizon.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I also reduce tree complexity and increase minimum child weight slightly so XGBoost is    │
│                          │ forced to prefer higher-support patterns that are less likely to evaporate in the         │
│                          │ validation regime. This should help raise val slope and pred_std_ratio without blowing up │
│                          │ the train/val gap.                                                                        │
