                        Patch Metadata - Gen 15/150 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/1                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ regime_robust_short_windows                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the main failure mode: the model’s signal collapses in the validation   │
│                          │ regime because it is learning overly specific level-based patterns and is too constrained │
│                          │ to express a stable slope.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I’m making two coordinated changes:                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Hyperparameters:                                                                       │
│                          │    - Relax regularization a bit so XGBoost can fit stronger but still controlled          │
│                          │ structure.                                                                                │
│                          │    - Increase tree count and depth slightly to recover predictive slope.                  │
│                          │    - Lower learning rate and raise early stopping patience to let the model find more     │
│                          │ robust patterns without overfitting sharply to the training regime.                       │
│                          │    - Keep min_child_weight above the current minimum to avoid noisy splits, but reduce it │
│                          │ from 5 to 2 to improve expressivity.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Features:                                                                              │
│                          │    - Shift emphasis toward short lookbacks and regime-normalized signals.                 │
│                          │    - Add rolling z-score versions of returns and volatility, which makes features more    │
│                          │ comparable across volatility regimes.                                                     │
│                          │    - Add trend-of-regime features such as vol_trend, efficiency_trend, and short-horizon  │
