│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ regime_delta_xgb                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This design is inspired by the earlier programs’ use of short-horizon momentum,           │
│                          │ volatility, efficiency, and interaction features, but it shifts the emphasis from “state” │
│                          │ features to “state change” features. The key idea is that the validation period appears   │
│                          │ to be a second regime shift, so absolute levels like volatility or trend strength are     │
│                          │ less useful than how those quantities are evolving.                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The novel part is a compact regime-delta feature set:                                     │
│                          │ - rolling z-scored price/volume/range features to reduce dependence on scale,             │
│                          │ - first-difference and slope features for volatility, efficiency, and order-flow proxies, │
│                          │ - regime-conditional interactions such as momentum × volatility-shift,                    │
│                          │ - a small number of orthogonalized short lookbacks to preserve responsiveness without     │
│                          │ overfitting,                                                                              │
│                          │ - slightly more expressive XGBoost settings with stronger sample constraints to prevent   │
│                          │ memorization while still allowing nonlinearity.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Overall, this is a regime-transition detector rather than a static regime classifier,     │
│                          │ which should help recover slope on the most recent period while keeping prediction        │
│                          │ dispersion above the collapse threshold.                                                  │
