│ patch_name               │ regime_shortlook_xgb                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover version keeps the stronger regime-stabilizing ideas from the prior         │
│                          │ implementations while reducing reliance on long lookbacks that likely caused the          │
│                          │ train→validation slope collapse. It emphasizes:                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - shorter rolling windows and faster-decaying signals,                                    │
│                          │ - rolling z-score normalization to make features more regime-invariant,                   │
│                          │ - explicit features for changes in market character such as volatility trend,             │
│                          │ autocorrelation trend, and efficiency trend,                                              │
│                          │ - a small number of interaction terms that often generalize better than raw components    │
│                          │ alone,                                                                                    │
│                          │ - slightly less regularization and a bit more model expressivity to reduce prediction     │
│                          │ collapse.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The feature count stays well under the 80-feature limit, all features use only past data, │
│                          │ and the interface/output format remains unchanged.                                        │
