                        Patch Metadata - Gen 22/150 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/1                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ regime_shift_xgb                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover keeps the strongest parts of both prior implementations while shifting the │
│                          │ feature set toward shorter, regime-invariant windows. The main changes are:               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - shorter lookbacks for returns, volatility, RSI, trend, and volume normalization         │
│                          │ - rolling z-score features to reduce sensitivity to absolute market regime                │
│                          │ - explicit “change in market character” features such as volatility trend, efficiency     │
│                          │ trend, and autocorrelation trend                                                          │
│                          │ - multiplicative interactions between momentum and volatility regime to capture           │
│                          │ conditional behavior                                                                      │
│                          │ - slightly more expressive XGBoost settings with controlled regularization so predictions │
│                          │ do not collapse toward the mean                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The feature count stays comfortably below the 80-feature limit, all features use only     │
│                          │ past data, and the run_experiment interface is unchanged.                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
