│ patch_description        │ This edit targets the two main failure modes: slope collapse on the validation regime and │
│                          │ prediction collapse toward the mean.                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ On the model side, I reduce over-regularization and use a slightly shallower but more     │
│                          │ persistent booster so XGBoost can retain signal without memorizing train-specific quirks. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ On the feature side, I replace the current broader state-feature mix with a more compact  │
│                          │ set centered on:                                                                          │
│                          │ - short lookbacks only                                                                    │
│                          │ - rolling z-scores for regime invariance                                                  │
│                          │ - rate-of-change features for market character                                            │
│                          │ - explicit change-of-character signals                                                    │
│                          │ - a few multiplicative interactions, especially momentum × volatility regime              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is designed to improve val slope and pred_std_ratio while keeping feature count well │
│                          │ below the 80-feature limit and maintaining past-only computation.                         │
