│ patch_description        │ This crossover version combines the strongest parts of the recent regime-adaptive feature │
│                          │ set with the most robust short-lookback ideas from the inspiration program.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Uses shorter windows and rolling z-scores to reduce regime dependence.                  │
│                          │ - Adds rate-of-change features for volatility, momentum, and efficiency to capture        │
│                          │ second-order regime shifts.                                                               │
│                          │ - Keeps a compact but expressive feature set well below the 80-feature limit.             │
│                          │ - Loosens regularization slightly versus the current program to reduce prediction         │
│                          │ collapse and raise prediction dispersion.                                                 │
│                          │ - Preserves the same interface, inputs, outputs, and causal-only feature construction.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The goal is to improve val slope and correlation without regressing the current           │
│                          │ directional accuracy.                                                                     │
